post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Google Drive for Omarchy Files is installed.

Connect an account:
  omarchy-gdrive-setup

Add more accounts from Files: right-click an empty area and choose
"Add Google Drive Account…" (needs nautilus-python).

Each account is mounted at ~/GoogleDrive/<email> and listed in the Files
sidebar under its email address.

Files loads extensions at startup, so restart it once after installing:
  nautilus --quit

The first run opens a browser for Google authorization and creates the
mount point, the bookmark, and a systemd user service per account.

For reliable access, configure your own OAuth client:
  https://rclone.org/drive/#making-your-own-client-id
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Google Drive for Omarchy Files was upgraded to account-named mounts.

Run the setup once to migrate:
  omarchy-gdrive-setup

It stops the old service, unmounts ~/GoogleDrive, recreates the mount at
~/GoogleDrive/<email>, and rewrites the bookmark and the systemd unit.
Until you run it, the sidebar still points at the old ~/GoogleDrive entry.

Restart Files to load the new "Add Google Drive Account…" menu item:
  nautilus --quit
EOF
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Per-user data is not removed automatically:
  - ~/GoogleDrive/<email>            (one folder per account)
  - ~/.config/omarchy-gdrive/accounts.tsv
  - ~/.config/rclone/rclone.conf
  - ~/.config/systemd/user/rclone-*.service
  - the account email bookmarks in ~/.config/gtk-3.0/bookmarks
See /usr/share/doc/omarchy-gdrive/README.md for cleanup steps.
EOF
}
